// Surface fold-in — the gradual top `?` as a type atom (gandr-89k).
//
// GRADUATION: the semantics LANDED with this fixture's change — strict and
// total lowering, session typing, and kernel admission all consume the atom —
// so the behavior is witnessed by the `gandr-surface-engine` lowering,
// session, and kernel tests. This fixture stays parse-only because its job is
// the SPELLING surface: `?` is the one unknown-type spelling on both sorts,
// with the consuming position deciding the sort, and the melder must keep
// three readings of the same tile disjoint — this atom, the Expression-sort
// typed hole (`?` / `?name`), and the receive-session prefix (`?T.S`). The
// ruled alternative to overloading the term-hole spelling: a structurally
// distinct atom, so host escapes and nested conditional bodies keep their
// existing CST fields. The legacy `Unknown` keyword stays a value-position
// primitive beside it, and the formatter canonicalizes every unknown back to
// `?`.

// Bare ascription: the sort-free signature position takes the value default.
def anything : ?;

// The returner payload is a value position: `F ?` is the PURE returner over
// the value unknown, never the computation top. The legacy keyword spelling
// denotes the same type (the two lower identically).
def pure_unknown : F ?;
def legacy_pure_unknown : F Unknown;

// Computation positions: arrow result, thunk body, lazy-product member.
def partial : Integer -> ?;
def suspended : U ?;
def choice : F Unit & ?;

// Value positions: product member (a `?`-led infix — the atom completes and
// the `*` continues the type) and arrow parameter.
def pair_left : ? * Integer;
def takes_unknown : ? -> F Unit;

// Parentheses are transparent: `(?)` is the same atom.
def parenthesized : Integer -> (?);

// The receive-session prefix keeps its own `?`-led reading: a type, `.`, and
// a session tail following the `?` selects `?T.S`, never the atom.
def session_receive : ? Integer . end;

// The Expression-sort typed hole is untouched beside the type atom.
def term_hole = ?;
def named_term_hole = ?goal;
